# Critical Rules (NO EXCEPTIONS)

- **npm only** — never pnpm or yarn
- **Schema first**: always check `database/schema.sql` before any SQL; never assume column names
- **Never edit `database/schema.sql` directly for schema changes** — write a migration in `database/migrations/` first, apply it, then update `schema.sql` to match
- **API monolith**: all required API logic stays **inline** in `api/index.ts` (Vercel serverless). Do **not** runtime-import from `shared/` or `server/` — `import type` only. Relative runtime modules break prod with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`
- **New API work goes in `api/index.ts`**, not legacy `server/`
- **Admin JWT** on all `/api/admin/*` except `/api/admin/auth/*`
- **No DocuSign** — contracts use the in-app signature canvas + QR check-in
- **Redux only for data**: never axios/fetch in components; use `createAsyncThunk` in slices; components only dispatch + select
- **Fix root causes** — never patch around type errors or bugs
- **No breaking changes**
- **Email is Resend** (`RESEND_API_KEY` + `SMTP_FROM`) — do not add Nodemailer/SMTP transports
- **API + swagger**: if `api/swagger.yaml` exists, update it when routes/behavior change
- **Design system**: relevant UI changes → update `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`
- **Review chat history** before changing code so you do not reintroduce fixed issues
- Prefer reusable components/utilities when it avoids debt
- Frontend: mobile-responsive, clean UX; UI logs via `client/lib/logger.ts`
